; =====================================================================
; QSMC — professional-execution preset (EA: QSMC_AutoTrader)
;
; WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
; The indicator reads the market well: structure, liquidity sweeps,
; displacement, order blocks, FVGs, premium/discount, targets. What it
; does NOT do is behave like a professional at the moment of taking the
; trade: it has no session window, no daily entry cap, no cooldown after
; a loss, and it either takes the whole target or nothing. Those four
; habits are not analysis, they are discipline, and they belong in the
; execution layer — this preset sets them.
;
; THE PRESET DOES NOT ARM THE ACCOUNT. InpEnableTrading stays false and
; InpDryRun stays true. Load it, read the journal lines for a few days,
; then walk the INERT -> DRY RUN -> demo ladder in
; docs/QSMC_GO_LIVE_RUNBOOK.md.
;
; THE VALUES AND WHY
;   session 07:00-20:00 server  covers London open through the NY
;                               afternoon; the hours where the indicator's
;                               own kill zones live. CHANGE THIS to your
;                               broker's server offset - open a chart, look
;                               at the clock in the Market Watch window, and
;                               compare it with your own time.
;   max 3 entries / day         a professional takes a few good trades, not
;                               every setup. Three is generous for a 4H
;                               model; it stops a chop day from revenge-
;                               trading a small account to zero.
;   cooldown 60 min             after a losing close. No re-entry inside the
;                               hour: the market did not change because you
;                               were stopped out, but your judgement did.
;   partial 50% at +1.00R       bank half at the first clean R, move the stop
;                               to entry (InpBreakEvenAtR=1.00, already the
;                               default). The rest rides to the indicator's
;                               target. This converts "right but stopped at
;                               break-even" from a loss of opportunity into
;                               a small win.
;
; HOW TO LOAD
;   1. Attach QSMC_AutoTrader to a chart, open its Properties -> Inputs.
;   2. Press "Load" and pick this file.
;   3. Press OK. The Experts journal prints one "discipline:" line with all
;      four values — if that line does not match this file, you loaded a
;      different preset.
;
; Every value below is an EXECUTION setting. None of them changes what the
; indicator detects; reload the chart afterwards and the analysis is
; identical.
; =====================================================================

InpEnableTrading=false
InpDryRun=true

InpSessionStartHour=7
InpSessionEndHour=20
InpMaxTradesPerDay=3
InpCooldownAfterLossMin=60
InpPartialCloseAtR=1.0
InpPartialClosePercent=50.0
InpBreakEvenAtR=1.00
